    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i had the flu like 3 weeks ago and finally felt better but now i'm feeling super weird. like i'm just completely wiped out and get really winded just walking up a few stairs. also my heart feels like it's fluttering or racing sometimes and there's this heavy feeling in my chest when i move around. is this just like long term fatigue from being sick or should i be worried?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "These symptoms could indicate Long COVID or another cardiac issue that requires medical evaluation. Missing the \"feeling better\" window usually suggests lingering effects of whatever you had, but sudden heart fluttering and chest tightness during movement are not typical for simple post-illness fatigue. I highly recommend seeing your doctor promptly to get your heart checked with an ECG and possibly a blood test.",
